  "description": "UJEHAU01 crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P -4 21 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C148 H112 N12 Nd8 O44 Si1. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2A (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd1F (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2F (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd1G (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2G (Nd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.862-4.583 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.29-125.50°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd8L8(C6H4NH2COO)4SiO4] (C148H112N12Nd8O44Si).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
